AtiSim — scope of the MIT licence
=================================

`LICENSE` covers the AtiSim source code, its documentation, and the data this
project derived itself — including the digitisations under
`Reference_papers/CR-2144/` and `atisim/data/`.

It does NOT cover the third-party reference documents this project reads, nor
the published figures and tables digitised from them. Those remain the property
of their publishers.

Reference documents
-------------------

Third-party documents are NOT redistributed in this repository. Seven are kept
because each is a US Government work, or prints the Title 17 statement that no
copyright is asserted in the United States, or states that it is not subject to
US copyright protection. The basis for each is recorded beside it in
`.gitignore`.

`Reference_papers/SOURCES.md` is the index: every document the project uses,
with its md5, its licence basis, and a permanent locator (DOI or NTRS ID) for
the ones not held here. Scripts that read a PDF take a `--pdf` path argument, so
they work against a copy you obtain yourself.

Digitised data
--------------

Data digitised from US Government works carries no separate restriction:

  - NASA CR-2144 (Boeing 747 aerodynamic data)
  - NASA TM-102186 (Wingrove & Bach, airline flight records)
  - Parks et al. 1985, J. Aircraft 22(2) — printed as public domain
  - MIL-F-8785C
  - AFFDL-TR-70-101 (HICAT) — approved for public release

Anything read from a publisher-held document is recorded in `docs/PROJECT.md`
as a citation to the table it came from, rather than reproduced.

Reference engine
----------------

`atisim/tests/data/jsbsim_*.xml` are frozen outputs generated from JSBSim
(github.com/JSBSim-Team/jsbsim), which is licensed under the LGPL 2.1. They are
generated data used as a comparison baseline, not JSBSim source. JSBSim itself
is an optional extra (`pip install -e .[ref]`) and is imported by exactly one
script; the test suite reads the frozen XML instead.
